arguments.prompt:
You are implementing a Blazor Web App for shipment tracking. The project has already been scaffolded at `/tmp/sv-a6e087b5a7ab4404b0cc9f2a5bb634c4/ShipmentTracker/` using `dotnet new blazor -o ShipmentTracker -int Auto -ai -au Individual`.

The project has two sub-projects:
- `ShipmentTracker/` (server) — hosts the app, has EF Core + Identity
- `ShipmentTracker.Client/` (WebAssembly) — all interactive components go here

## Architecture (Auto mode rules)
- Interactive components MUST go in `.Client` project
- `.Client` components cannot access DbContext directly — must use HTTP APIs
- Define shared interfaces/models in `.Client` project
- Server implements the interface with direct DB access; Client implements with HttpClient
- Register matching service implementations in both Program.cs files
- API endpoints on the server for the client HttpClient to call

## What to implement

### 1. Shared Models in `.Client` project

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/ShipmentDto.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public enum ShipmentStatus
{
    Pending,
    PickedUp,
    InTransit,
    OutForDelivery,
    Delivered,
    Cancelled
}

public class ShipmentDto
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }
    public DateTime CreatedAt { get; set; }
    public DateTime? EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public DateTime? ActualDelivery { get; set; }
    public string RecipientName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
```

### 2. Service Interface in `.Client` project

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/IShipmentService.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public interface IShipmentService
{
    Task<List<ShipmentDto>> GetShipmentsAsync(string? statusFilter = null, string? searchTerm = null);
    Task<ShipmentDto?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber);
    Task<ShipmentDto?> GetShipmentByIdAsync(int id);
    Task<ShipmentDto> UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus newStatus);
}
```

### 3. Client-side HttpClient implementation

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/HttpShipmentService.cs`:
```csharp
using System.Net.Http.Json;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

public class HttpShipmentService(HttpClient httpClient) : IShipmentService
{
    public async Task<List<ShipmentDto>> GetShipmentsAsync(string? statusFilter = null, string? searchTerm = null)
    {
        var query = new List<string>();
        if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(statusFilter)) query.Add($"status={Uri.EscapeDataString(statusFilter)}");
        if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(searchTerm)) query.Add($"search={Uri.EscapeDataString(searchTerm)}");
        var url = "api/shipments" + (query.Count > 0 ? "?" + string.Join("&", query) : "");
        return await httpClient.GetFromJsonAsync<List<ShipmentDto>>(url) ?? [];
    }

    public async Task<ShipmentDto?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        var response = await httpClient.GetAsync($"api/shipments/track/{Uri.EscapeDataString(trackingNumber)}");
        if (!response.IsSuccessStatusCode) return null;
        return await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<ShipmentDto>();
    }

    public async Task<ShipmentDto?> GetShipmentByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        var response = await httpClient.GetAsync($"api/shipments/{id}");
        if (!response.IsSuccessStatusCode) return null;
        return await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<ShipmentDto>();
    }

    public async Task<ShipmentDto> UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus newStatus)
    {
        var response = await httpClient.PutAsJsonAsync($"api/shipments/{id}/status", newStatus);
        response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
        return (await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<ShipmentDto>())!;
    }
}
```

### 4. Server-side EF Core Entity

Create `ShipmentTracker/Data/Shipment.cs`:
```csharp
using System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Data;

public class Shipment
{
    public int Id { get; set; }

    [MaxLength(20)]
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [MaxLength(200)]
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [MaxLength(200)]
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    public int Status { get; set; }

    public DateTime CreatedAt { get; set; }
